 ## Overview
-The TensoRF Training Loop is the iterative optimization procedure used to fit the tensorial radiance field parameters to a set of multi-view images [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of minimizing the difference between rendered pixel colors and ground truth observations by performing gradient descent on the decomposed tensor components [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from standard NeRF optimization by operating on low-rank tensor factors (vector and matrix components) rather than a dense MLP, requiring specific regularization terms (orthogonal, L1, and Total Variation) to maintain the structural integrity and smoothness of the tensor decomposition [S1, unofficial].
+The TensoRF Training Loop is the iterative optimization procedure used to minimize the L2 rendering loss of a tensorial radiance field, using ground truth pixel colors as supervision [S1, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from standard NeRF training by incorporating specific regularization terms (orthogonal, L1 density, and Total Variation) tailored to the low-rank tensor decomposition structure, alongside a dynamic alpha mask update mechanism [S1, unofficial].
 
