 ## Background
-TensoRF was introduced in the paper "Tensorial Radiance Fields" (ECCV 2022) [S1, unofficial]. It represents the radiance field as a tensor decomposition, enabling efficient storage and rendering [S1, unofficial]. The training loop incorporates specific regularization techniques to handle the low-rank constraints, distinguishing it from standard NeRF optimization which uses an MLP [S1, unofficial].
+The TensoRF Training Loop originates from the TensoRF paper (ECCV 2022) [S1, unofficial]. It is used in conjunction with various extensions such as NeuManifold, Joint Pose Optimization, StyleTRF, and PATA [S1, S2, S3, unofficial].
 
